-- replay --
$ dorc --book=book.sh --pre-source package.oracle.sh --results - < probe-results.txt
#!/bin/sh
# dorc probe (read-only): checks per-SITE convergence, mutates nothing.
# When run, emits one results-record per site on stdout (the return channel):
#   site <leafid> effect=<holds|absent|cant-tell> rc=<n>
# effect is derived from the probe command's rc (0=holds, 1=absent, else cant-tell);
# rc is the raw PROBE-command status (opaque to Dorc -- the record is the out-of-band lane).

printf 'dorc-records/1 nonce=dorc attempt=1 host=localhost book=ee7260bfdf663a31a9c57a4c3d58f204ab4ccc3eb330502d4a00ab73859e8f92 sites=1 @@dorc@@\n'
# site 1: sm.dorc.Package:nginx@installed
apt_get__is_converged() {
   while [ "${1#-}" != "$1" ]; do shift; done
   verb=$1; shift
   while [ "${1#-}" != "$1" ]; do shift; done
   case $verb in
      install) dpkg-query -W "$1" >/dev/null 2>&1 ;;
   esac
}
apt_get__is_converged 'install' '-y' 'nginx'; _rc=$?; if [ "$_rc" -eq 0 ]; then _e=holds; elif [ "$_rc" -eq 1 ]; then _e=absent; else _e=cant-tell; fi; printf 'dorc site 1 effect=%s rc=%s @@dorc@@\n' "$_e" "$_rc"
# site:0 unresolvable-no-probe
printf 'dorc-records-end/1 nonce=dorc @@dorc@@\n'
probe: note[site-unresolvable]: sm 1 site run unprobed (no read-only check could
be shipped): `hork wombat` -- run `dorc why` for the per-site detail (the apply
runs each anyway, to stay safe)
      [ book.sh:2:1
   2 | hork wombat
     | \_________/

   = help:  sm site runs `hork wombat`
why: site 1 guard refused -- the site's structurally-awkward form (a heredoc body, or a non-`/dev/null` output redirect) would corrupt the artifact or suppress an admin-spelled side-effect, so the original bytes RUN VERBATIM (to stay safe), the sm.dorc.Package oracle's vouch that it is already satisfied notwithstanding
hint: 'hork' (line 2) is unmodeled: it is the first wall -- an oracle vouching its convergence would elide it when converged, and un-wall 1 downstream site
dorc: run `dorc why` for the per-site cause-chains, or `dorc why book.sh:N` to query a source line
render: error[render-heredoc-refused]: Dorc cannot guard `apt-get install -y
nginx <<EOF` as planned: rewriting the line would strand the heredoc body below
its `<<` opener, so the command stays in place and runs verbatim.
      [ book.sh:3:1
   3 | apt-get install -y nginx <<EOF
     | \____________________________/

   = help:  Move the heredoc's content out of the command -- feed it with printf
            or redirect from a file -- and Dorc can then elide or guard the
            site.
